man - the manual

SYNOPSIS
    man [PAGE]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints a manual page, through less when there is a terminal to page onto
    and straight out when there is not - so `man ls | grep -i sort` works.

    With no argument, lists every page there is.

    The pages are plain text, not troff. troff is a typesetting language, and
    the reason manual pages are written in it is that in 1971 the same source
    had to drive a phototypesetter. What is left when that goes is a file
    anybody can read with cat.

SEE ALSO
    less, help
